   "text": "Temple University - QS Apply\nSkip to main content\nHOMEPAGE\nAPPLICATIONS\nNOTIFICATIONS\nEK\nTemple University\nSummary\nDegrees and Programs\nStudent Testimonials\nCommission\nViewer Access\nAny user can see this institution.\nDescription\nFounded as a night school by Russell Conwell in 1884, Temple University has evolved into an international powerhouse in higher education and a top research institution with roughly 33,000 undergraduate, graduate and professional students. Philadelphia’s public university, Temple provides an unparalleled value to families in the region and serves as an essential resource to the surrounding community. \nTimestamps\nUpdated\n26/03/2026 07:29\nby Eston Dalmeida\nCreated\n26/03/2026 07:29\nby Eston Dalmeida\nType\nUniversity\nPREMIUM INSTITUTION\nCountry\nUnited States\nYearly Fees\nMax: US$30,528.00\nMin: US$30,150.00\nInternational Students\nPercentage of International Students\n6%\n1,831 of 30,530 Total Students\nOverview\nBasic Details\nInstitution Details\nOwnership\nPublic\nProvider\nDirect QS\nFounded Year\n1884\nCampus(es)\nPhiladelphia\nCountry\nUnited States\nExcluded Countries\nNA\nPREMIUM INSTITUTION\n Yes\nContract Start Date\n26/01/2023\nContract End Date\n01/01/2036\nContract Entity\nQSSA Ltd\nContract Status\nActive\nContract Document Link(s)\nN/A\nImages\nImages\nAdditional Details\nAccommodation Details\nhttps://offcampus.temple.edu/\nScholarship Offered\nUp to $10.000 for qualified international applicants.\nCriteria include a minimum GPA of 3.0 and performance in the subject area over the last two years. Students are automatically evaluated for eligibility when they apply, no separate application needed. Scholarship offers are sent separately from admission letters within a similar timeframe.\nYouTube Video Link(s)\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RFeFhJyRrfM\nInternship Details\nhttps://careercenter.temple.edu/students/grow/tuip-%E2%80%93-temple-university-internship-program\nhttps://careercenter.temple.edu/students/grow/internships\nAdditional Information\n-",
